1302:[{"file":"packages/core/src/agent/loop.ts","line":898,"severity":"P1","finding":"The full maxOutputTokens limit is sent without reserving space for the prompt. Compaction permits input up to 80% of the context window, while inferred output limits can consume 25% or more, so otherwise valid long sessions can be rejected because prompt tokens plus max output exceed the model context window.","suggested_fix":"Compute the request budget from the remaining context, including system/tool overhead, or lower the compaction threshold to reserve maxOutputTokens; add a near-context-limit test."},{"file":"packages/providers/src/local/openai-compat.ts","line":120,"severity":"P1","finding":"The broad /gemma/i heuristic assigns a 131072-token context to every Gemma model, including older and small checkpoints with much smaller windows. This suppresses required compaction and eventually sends over-context requests. The generic Qwen heuristic has the same risk for older checkpoints.","suggested_fix":"Use version/checkpoint-specific heuristics only where the minimum context is known; otherwise retain the conservative default and require server metadata or a model override. Add tests for older/small Gemma and Qwen IDs."},{"file":"packages/providers/src/registry.ts","line":228,"severity":"P2","finding":"Model overrides are applied only during initial registry construction. refresh() replaces all local models with newly discovered entries without reapplying config.models, so the new authoritative contextWindow, maxOutputTokens, and reasoning corrections silently disappear after a refresh.","suggested_fix":"Extract override application into a helper and invoke it after both initial discovery and refresh; add a refresh test for a custom local model override."},{"file":"packages/providers/src/local/openai-compat.ts","line":188,"severity":"P2","finding":"Embedding models are recognized as non-chat models but are still registered as available with conversation/simple-edit affinities. The router filters toolCalling=false only for tool-requiring tasks, so a simple conversation can select an embedding model and send it to streamText with a one-token output budget.","suggested_fix":"Exclude embedding-only entries from the chat model registry, or add an explicit chat-generation capability that routing enforces; test discovery/routing when an endpoint lists both chat and embedding models."}]
